    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hipatterns\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, there are a few tunable options for the highlights that are passed into the `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmarks` function ([here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua#L775), [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua#L792), and [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua#L794)). There are actually a lot of possible options that could allow for highlighting the entire line, setting virtual text, or replacing/masking the text (list of options for extmarks [here](https://neovim.io/doc/user/api.html#nvim_buf_set_extmark())).\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to expose this `extmark_opts` table to make these options accessible? The `priority` option is already available [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L178), so exposing all the options could be a simple as adding an `extmark_opts` config to `highlighters` with `priority` inside or as a separate table.\r\n\r\nHappy to submit a PR if this seems a worthwhile feature.",
