        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Oh, after sleeping on it, I decided to try to go through with it. I have a working solution which I'll revise tomorrow. It will have ability to supply both table and function as `extmark_opts`. It is just indeed provides many opportunities with a small change. And judging by the brief tests, performance should not take a huge hit.\r\n\r\nI am not sure yet about deprecating `priority`, as it will be a breaking change though.\r\n\r\nDo you have a particular use case for using `hl_eol` before I finalize design of `extmark_opts`? Because right now it can be used, but highlighting still starts at the start of the pattern match, so no way to highlight whole line containing some match.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: I mean, highlighting whole line *can* be solved by starting pattern with `'^.*'`, but it might be not very performant. Still should be OK, though.",
